1. HAETAE reference implementation
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This work builds on the HAETAE digital signature reference implementation by
the HAETAE team (CryptoLab) and its Cortex-M4 port in pqm4
(https://github.com/mupq/pqm4). The files listed here are included UNMODIFIED
from the HAETAE reference (verified byte-identical against those upstream
sources) and
remain the work of the HAETAE authors, under the original HAETAE license:

  api.h            ntt.c          poly_sparsemul.h    sign.h
  arm_simd.h       ntt.h          randombytes.c       stack_profile.c
  decompose.c      ntt332.h       randombytes.h       stack_profile.h
  decompose.h      ntt332.S       reduce.c            symmetric.h
  fast_exp_asm.h   m4.h           reduce.h            symmetric-shake.c
  fast_exp_asm.S   params.h       fixpoint.c          utils.c
  fast_sampler.S   polymat.c      fixpoint.h          utils.h
  fpa.h            polymat.h      verify.h

These files are left as-is (no Apache 2.0 header). Classification is per file and
per port: a given basename may be byte-identical to the HAETAE reference in one
port (no header, listed above) yet modified for our low-stack / streaming work in
another port (and there it carries our Apache 2.0 header). The authoritative
signal is the presence or absence of the Apache 2.0 header at the top of each
individual file.


